                        <item_1571070731882
                            cq:panelTitle="Who is Weekender for?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-14T09:32:49.895-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:16:36.508-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p>For anyone with a free weekend and some curiosity. Every trip says plainly how fit and how experienced you need to be, and many need no experience at all. We write for people who have done these things for years and for people who are about to try them for the first time.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                        </item_1571070731882>
                        <item_1
                            cq:panelTitle="How does Weekender earn its money?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            jcr:title="Item 1"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-14T09:51:23.154-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:17:16.517-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p>From the trips. The price of a trip pays the guides, the places we stay and the people who plan it. Nobody pays to appear in the magazine, and a trip is not listed higher because someone paid for it.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h3>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                        </item_1>
                        <item_2
                            cq:panelTitle="Can I write for Weekender?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            jcr:title="Item 2"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-14T10:12:29.401-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:17:39.663-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p>Yes. If you know a place well and can describe it honestly, send us a short outline of the story and a few photographs of your own. We answer every proposal, and we pay for what we publish.&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                        </item_2>
                        <item_1571070705187
                            cq:panelTitle="How often is there something new?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-14T10:12:54.254-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:18:11.562-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p>A new story appears in the magazine about once a week, and new trips are added at the start of each season. The dates and prices of the trips are kept up to date all year.&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                        </item_1571070705187>
                        <item_1571070718887
                            cq:panelTitle="How did Weekender start?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-14T10:13:09.156-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:18:36.836-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p>With a shared spreadsheet. A few friends kept a list of weekend trips they had liked, with notes on what to bring and where to eat afterwards, and the list was passed on so often that it became a website. The trips with guides came later, when readers began to ask whether they could come along.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                        </item_1571070718887>
                        <item_1572027287775
                            cq:panelTitle="What if the weather is bad?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-25T11:18:51.723-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:19:08.411-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p>Then the guide changes the plan. Every trip has a second route for bad days, and a guide may shorten or move a day for the safety of the group. If we have to cancel a trip ourselves, you get your money back.&lt;/p>&#xa;"
                                textIsRich="true"/>
                        </item_1572027287775>
                        <item_1572027298182
                            cq:panelTitle="Is Weekender a real company?"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/container">
                            <text
                                jcr:created="{Date}2019-10-25T11:19:22.144-07:00"
                                jcr:createdBy="admin"
                                jcr:lastModified="{Date}2019-10-25T11:19:41.501-07:00"
                                jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                sling:resourceType="weekender/components/text"
                                text="&lt;p&gt;No. Weekender is a fictional online magazine and adventure company that focuses on outdoor activities and trips across the globe. The site is the demo of Sensible Studio: it shows what a site built from components, templates and content fragments looks like, and what authors do with it. It started from the WKND reference site by Adobe, published under the MIT licence.&lt;/p&gt;"
                                textIsRich="true">
                                <cq:responsive jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured">
                                    <default
                                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                        offset="0"
                                        width="12"/>
                                </cq:responsive>
                            </text>
                        </item_1572027298182>
